# ===========================================================================
# Netlify headers
#
# /p/12 gets proxied through to the Supabase function, and it responds with
# text/html. Netlify still serves it as text/plain: when proxying, it guesses
# the type from the file extension in the path, and /p/12 has none. The
# browser then shows the raw source instead of the page, the redirect never
# fires, and X's crawler cannot find the meta lines.
#
# Measured, not guessed:
#   curl -sI https://sized.gg/p/16                        -> text/plain
#   curl -sI https://<project>.supabase.co/.../og/p/16    -> text/html
#
# This file only takes effect when it sits in the root directory of the
# uploaded site - next to index.html.
# ===========================================================================

# ===========================================================================
# The security headers
#
# IMPORTANT - fill in before uploading:
#
# In connect-src below, DEIN-PROJEKT appears twice. It needs the real
# project address there, or the site cannot reach its own database and
# shows nothing at all. Same step as in _redirects:
#
#   cd <project-folder>
#   URL=$(grep -o 'https://[a-z0-9]*\.supabase\.co' public/config.js | head -1)
#   HOST=${URL#https://}
#   perl -pi -e "s{wbkfjvpxxlwcivqcmmpo\.supabase\.co}{$HOST}g" public/_headers
#   grep connect-src public/_headers
#
# The last line shows what is there now - it must no longer say
# "DEIN-PROJEKT".
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What each line does, and why it's set this way and not stricter
#
# default-src 'none'
#   Nothing is allowed except what is explicitly listed below. Anything that
#   got forgotten breaks and does not work - better that way round than
#   a gap nobody notices.
#
# script-src 'self'
#   Only scripts from sized.gg itself. No 'unsafe-inline', no CDN. This is
#   the line that matters: it's the one that makes injected code
#   harmless. The site has not a single inline script and loads
#   supabase-js from public/vendor/, so this strictness costs nothing here.
#
# style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'
#   'unsafe-inline' is set here, and that is a tradeoff, not
#   carelessness. A poll's bar width is set as
#   style="width:61.8%" in the markup (app.js, in pollHtml). Without
#   'unsafe-inline' every bar would sit at zero.
#
#   The rework is possible - set the width via JavaScript after
#   inserting the markup - but pollHtml is reused verbatim by thirteen
#   scripts, and each one would need the new call added. Miss one and it
#   silently shows empty bars.
#
#   What 'unsafe-inline' actually opens up for style: injected CSS. That
#   requires someone to be able to inject markup at all (everything
#   inserted runs through esc()), and the usual way to exfiltrate data
#   with it - background: url(https://attacker-address/...) - is blocked
#   anyway by default-src 'none'. Scripts stay strict, and that's where
#   the real damage would be.
#
# img-src 'self' data: blob:
#   data: for the icon in the address bar, which sits as an SVG directly
#   in index.html. blob: for the images the site itself builds from a
#   poll.
#
# connect-src 'self' https://... wss://...
#   The database and the live connection. wss:// is not optional - without
#   the second address DMs stop arriving, and you would only see it in
#   production.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none' (and X-Frame-Options repeating it for older
#   browsers): nobody can put sized.gg inside an invisible frame and
#   hijack clicks. On a site where people cast votes in Ansem's polls,
#   that is not theoretical.
#
# base-uri 'none' / form-action 'none' / object-src 'none'
#   Three paths nobody needs, and through which redirects would
#   otherwise be possible.
#
# Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
#   Clicking the X link does not tell the other side which page it came
#   from. This is the line that belongs to "nobody should be able to
#   find the name".
#
# Strict-Transport-Security
#   Two years, all subdomains. WITHOUT preload, and deliberately so: preload
#   adds the domain to a list that ships baked into the browsers
#   themselves, and getting off it again takes months. Once sized.gg has
#   been up for a year, that can be added.
#
# Permissions-Policy
#   Camera, microphone, location, motion sensors, payments: the site
#   needs none of it, so it never asks for any of it.
#
# What is deliberately MISSING: Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy. Set to
# same-origin, it could stop X's card preview from fetching og-karte.png -
# and the card is half the reason a shared link is worth anything. The
# gain would not be worth it.
# ===========================================================================

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://wbkfjvpxxlwcivqcmmpo.supabase.co wss://wbkfjvpxxlwcivqcmmpo.supabase.co; manifest-src 'self'; worker-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# ===========================================================================
# /p/* needs NO CSP of its own - measured on September 3, 2026
#
# A separate, looser rule sat here briefly, with the reasoning: the og
# function serves a page with an inline script, and the strict rule
# above (script-src 'self') would block that. Both parts were wrong.
#
# What actually comes back:
#
#   curl -s -D - -o /dev/null 'https://sized.gg/p/16'
#   -> HTTP/2 302
#      location: https://sized.gg/#poll-16
#      content-length: 0
#      x-served-by: supabase-edge-runtime
#
# An empty redirect. No HTML, no script, nothing a CSP could
# block. The og function distinguishes: humans get a real 302, only
# crawlers get the page with the meta lines - and a crawler does not
# evaluate a CSP, it reads text. See the full explanation in
# supabase/functions/og/index.ts.
#
# Second finding from the same measurement: the response contains
#
#   strict-transport-security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
#
# That is NOT our value (above it's 63072000 without preload), it's
# Supabase's. Netlify does not add any headers from this file to a
# proxied response at all. This entire block has no effect.
#
# The Content-Type line stays anyway: it costs nothing, it was already
# here before, and if Netlify ever changes how it proxies, it will take
# effect again. Just don't assume it is doing anything right now.
# ===========================================================================

# ===========================================================================
# The font files
#
# They are immutable: the name carries the weight, and a different cut gets
# a different name. So the browser never has to ask again - a year is the
# maximum the standard allows, and "immutable" tells it not even to
# revalidate on a reload.
#
# Why this matters more here than for a picture: the font is on the critical
# path. Every figure on the page is drawn with it, and while it is being
# fetched the text is set in a fallback with different widths. Once is
# unavoidable. Once per visit would not be.
#
# If the font is ever replaced, the file has to get a new NAME - overwriting
# it under the same name would leave everyone who has been here before with
# the old one for a year.
# ===========================================================================

# ===========================================================================
# /check.html - die Messseite braucht zwei Adressen mehr
#
# Sie zeigt die oeffentliche Adresse des Geraets an, und das ist nicht
# Beiwerk: nur so sieht man, ob Handy und Rechner von aussen unter derselben
# Adresse auftauchen - sonst kann ein gruenes Ergebnis genau das bedeuten und
# die Schlussfolgerung ist falsch. Die zwei Dienste dafuer stehen nur HIER in
# connect-src und nicht in der Regel fuer die ganze Seite.
#
# Der Rest der Regel ist derselbe wie oben, absichtlich ausgeschrieben:
# Netlify ersetzt die Kopfzeile fuer diesen Pfad, es ergaenzt sie nicht.
# ===========================================================================

/check.html
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://wbkfjvpxxlwcivqcmmpo.supabase.co wss://wbkfjvpxxlwcivqcmmpo.supabase.co https://api.ipify.org https://ipapi.co; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/p/*
  Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8

